        "original_id": "507ae4a4-8006-5158-bacf-2a098cc8125e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking, New South Wales Government, New South Wales Police, Mafia, Honoured Society, 'Ndrangheta\n- Places: New South Wales, Australia, Melbourne\n\nFacts:\n- From 1977 to 1979, the Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking, also called the Wodward Royal Commission, operated as a royal commission.\n- The New South Wales Government initiated the Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking to investigate drug trafficking in New South Wales, Australia.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking especially investigated links between the New South Wales Police and the Mafia.\n- The Honoured Society is a Calabrian 'Ndrangheta criminal confederation.\n- The Honoured Society started in Melbourne and is currently active across Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
