        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking, Honoured Society, New South Wales Police, Mafia, 'Ndrangheta\n- Places: New South Wales, Australia, Melbourne\n- People: Donald Mackay\n- Events: Donald Mackay's disappearance\n- Topics: drug trafficking, organized crime\n\nFacts:\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking was a royal commission that operated from 1977 to 1979.\n- The New South Wales Government initiated the Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking to investigate drug trafficking in New South Wales, Australia.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking especially examined links between the Mafia and New South Wales Police.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking also investigated the disappearance of anti-marijuana campaigner Donald Mackay.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking was also known as the Woodward Royal Commission.\n- The Honoured Society is a Calabrian 'Ndrangheta criminal confederation.\n- The Honoured Society started in Melbourne and is currently active throughout Australia.",
